{
  "description": "Exact contractHash and registrationHash values (contract-document.md section 6). Each case gives a document and the two hashes a conformant implementation computes from it: build the projection P (section 6.2 steps 1-5), canonicalize with RFC 8785, SHA-256, lowercase hex, prefix 'sha256:'. Several cases are deliberately decorated, reordered, renamed, hoisted or annotated, and their expected values equal an undecorated case's - proving an implementation performs each normalization step rather than hashing its input verbatim. A case's document is the input as it stands; for the two projection cases it is already projected.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "minimal-document",
      "description": "One request entry, inline schemas, no events or sends.",
      "document": {
        "schemaDialect": "openapi-3.0",
        "service": "conformance",
        "requests": [
          {
            "topic": "orders:create",
            "request": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "orderId": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "orderId"
              ]
            },
            "response": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "status": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "status"
              ]
            }
          }
        ],
        "events": [],
        "sends": [],
        "components": {
          "schemas": {}
        }
      },
      "expectedContractHash": "sha256:2b8906d276bb0e6f24ed6f77d919841812903e0affdf611daa4cac42716dddc7",
      "expectedRegistrationHash": "sha256:ad398055f066b2917d168d6c4ab9097b5691351e83484d3b9816376558946013"
    },
